WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.730
- I've never let go of my vision.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.690
To commit to the commitment,

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:06.650
is very powerful.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.813
I only try to do one thing at a time.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.010
- Need motivation?

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.000
- What's your Top 10, with Believe Nation.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.550
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.700
I believe in you,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.880
and this channel is designed to be part

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.990
of your daily success routine.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.180
So, let's get your motivation to a 10,

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.090
and get you believing in you.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.810
Grab a snack, and chew
into today's lessons

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.690
from a woman who went from
being a anthropology student,

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.696
to dropping out of school
to become an actress,

00:00:34.696 --> 00:00:37.480
to becoming an Academy
Award Winning actress,

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.100
and successful entrepreneur.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.140
She's Gwyneth Paltrow,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.098
and here is my take on her
top 10 rules to success.

00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:46.681
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.680
Okay, let's kick it off
with rule number one,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.480
take risks.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.510
- You know for me, I took
a crazy risk, you know?

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.393
I really did have a
perfectly good day job.

00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:07.936
- [Man] It was really going well?

00:01:07.936 --> 00:01:09.333
- It was going great.

00:01:10.923 --> 00:01:11.756
- Were you nervous?

00:01:11.756 --> 00:01:13.360
Were you really scared to jump in,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.853
or what were you feeling?

00:01:14.853 --> 00:01:15.730
- I was scared,

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.150
but I had self belief.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.856
And that's what I think ultimately...

00:01:19.856 --> 00:01:22.480
Because people knock
you down all the time,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.570
and they poke holes,

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.720
and they don't like this
about your business model,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.020
and they don't believe in you.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.590
You know, you just have
to keep getting back up,

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.450
and getting back up,

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.410
and getting back up.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.280
And I think what got me through,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.092
was this I've never let go of my vision.

00:01:37.092 --> 00:01:39.440
It's like I just see a bulls eye,

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.270
and it might be really, really far away,

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.130
but I'm going straight for it,

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.018
and doing the best I can.

00:01:47.018 --> 00:01:48.900
But, in the meantime,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.180
I'm building a really
interesting business.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.580
- Rule number two, value time.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.600
- What's the best piece of advice

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.050
you've ever been given,

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.390
that you keep with you to this day?

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.190
- My dad gave me the best advice,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.670
pertaining to every situation.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.520
In my 20s, I was having trouble

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.760
with one of my girlfriends,

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.890
who I've known since grade school.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.740
And he said, "You can't
make new old friends."

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.250
And it really stuck with me.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.690
Now, that's actually a piece of advice

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.430
I think you can apply
it to other things too.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.460
It's like, the value in time,

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.370
you know it's sort of like
what you were saying with cash.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.240
The value that's created when two people

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.120
make a commitment,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.330
whether it's a relationship,

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.163
or a friendship,

00:02:29.163 --> 00:02:31.320
or a parent child relationship,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.170
to commit to the commitment
is very powerful.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.850
- It is very powerful.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.360
- Rule number three, like yourself.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.211
- What is the single most important thing

00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:43.570
that changed that you're grateful,

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:47.023
that you made when it
comes to your own wellness?

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.820
- I think deciding that I liked myself,

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.880
and that I didn't really ultimately...

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.510
It didn't serve me what other
people's opinions were of me,

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:02.343
good or bad,

00:03:02.343 --> 00:03:03.850
whatever that projection was

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.140
really wasn't serving me.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.140
And I think around the
time that I turned 40,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.560
I felt like I got a software upgrade.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.007
And I was like, "Oh,
I kind of like myself,

00:03:18.007 --> 00:03:19.473
"and I kind of don't give a."

00:03:20.707 --> 00:03:21.540
(laughing)

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.580
You know what I mean?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.670
I think it's a real blessing,

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.340
and I think everybody when they turn 40,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.110
gets this software upgrade

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.310
and it's been an incredible blessing.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.270
I think because with that

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.310
has come a lot of self-acceptance,

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.260
and forgiveness,

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.990
and being present and open,

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.380
and not fighting so hard against this idea

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.350
of what I thought I was supposed to be,

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.710
or where I was supposed to be,

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.080
or what kind of marriage
I was supposed to have,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.150
or X,Y and Z.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.650
I really accepted myself,

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.070
and that I think I feel so
much better having done that,

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:02.070
than I did from doing Yoga
and eating macrobiotic food.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.680
- Rule number four, build
something you believe in.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.200
- Has anything surprised you
about being an entrepreneur?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.033
Before you came in,

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:12.060
and you decided to fully
throw yourself all in?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.740
Anything surprised you
about this experience?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.390
- I mean, so many things surprise me.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:19.540
I had no idea what I was getting into,

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.570
I had no idea how much I didn't know,

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.392
and how much there was to learn.

00:04:23.392 --> 00:04:28.392
I had no idea how much I was in a career

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.656
where everyone kissed my ass,

00:04:30.656 --> 00:04:33.230
and now people are like well you.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.889
What's the bottom line?

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:35.722
(laughing)

00:04:35.722 --> 00:04:36.555
Like, oh.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.380
Now I'm like on jet blue.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.701
I'm like, "What the did I do here?"

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:42.870
(laughing)

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:47.030
But honestly, I've never felt
so professionally fulfilled

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:47.863
in my life,

00:04:47.863 --> 00:04:48.696
and it's such a grind,

00:04:48.696 --> 00:04:49.620
and it's such hard work,

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.580
but it's so amazing to
be building something

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.480
that you believe in,

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.250
and making product that you love,

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.560
and putting it into the world,

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.210
and getting feedback
positive and negative,

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.360
and sorting through it.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.180
I much prefer it,

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.810
even though no one kisses my ass anymore.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.170
- Rule number five, learn
how to deal with criticism.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.420
- So, this is what Martha Stewart

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.940
said about Gwyneth a couple of weeks ago.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.917
This was well before
the lease announcement.

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:18.097
"She just needs to be quiet,

00:05:18.097 --> 00:05:19.497
"she's a movie star.

00:05:19.497 --> 00:05:21.117
"If she were confident in her acting,

00:05:21.117 --> 00:05:23.802
"she wouldn't be trying
to be Martha Stewart."

00:05:23.802 --> 00:05:25.660
(laughing)

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.750
- First of all,

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:30.090
no one has ever said
anything bad about me before,

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:34.550
so I'm shocked and devastated.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:35.933
I'll try to recover.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.020
You know, if I'm really honest,

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:48.023
I am so psyched that she
sees us as competition.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.760
Like, I'm so psyched.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.903
I think that when anybody
criticizes anyone,

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:01.470
it really is just revealing
more about where they are

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.710
in time and space,

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.850
as opposed to where you
are in time and space.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.850
And I think generally we
tend to you know lash out,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.080
if we're in a...

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:13.913
You know what I mean?

00:06:13.913 --> 00:06:15.940
It's usually a reflection
of something else,

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.020
and so I try not to...

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.790
In this point in my life,

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.480
I don't take it personally.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.000
I see it as a projection,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.900
and you know if there's
ever anything that sticks,

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.720
then I know oh maybe I'm holding

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.170
this judgment against myself,

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.850
and I need to look at that.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.340
But, it's very interesting.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.064
And you know, sometimes I learn
good things from criticism.

00:06:42.064 --> 00:06:45.030
- Rule number six, start small.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.550
- I want to know about the first time

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.468
you set your finger tips to keyboard,

00:06:48.468 --> 00:06:51.760
and decided to start a weekly newsletter.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.004
- It really kind of came about

00:06:54.004 --> 00:06:55.710
in a very small way.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.210
Me in my kitchen with my girlfriends,

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.820
talking about ideas.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.120
And then, what started to happen,

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:06.290
was essentially there was a
trust that started to get built

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.350
between myself and my readers,

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:10.190
and there was a lot of traction

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.152
that started to happen.

00:07:12.152 --> 00:07:13.640
If I recommended something that I found,

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.500
or that I loved,

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.850
then I was starting to
have this amazing feedback

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.640
from these businesses saying this has

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.200
a real measurable, big impact.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.630
And I was like, "Oh wow,
that's interesting."

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.810
And so, it was kind of all piece by piece.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:32.730
It was a very slow, very
organic process over years.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.650
You know I've been doing
it for a really long time.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.937
Until I sort of started to think,

00:07:36.937 --> 00:07:41.377
"Well, I wonder how I would do this,

00:07:41.377 --> 00:07:43.997
"if I wanted to turn it into a business?

00:07:43.997 --> 00:07:45.417
"If I wanted to monetize it?

00:07:45.417 --> 00:07:46.437
"Do I want to do that?

00:07:46.437 --> 00:07:48.717
"Would I ever have advertising,

00:07:48.717 --> 00:07:50.212
"would I ever sell anything?

00:07:50.212 --> 00:07:51.879
"What would I sell?"

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.980
And the process just was a slow evolution.

00:07:56.980 --> 00:08:00.030
- Rule number seven, learn
through trial and error.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:00.863
- You know, what was the transition

00:08:00.863 --> 00:08:03.580
going from a huge Hollywood
actress, huge star,

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.550
to entrepreneur?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.383
How did you learn?

00:08:05.383 --> 00:08:06.580
Did you kind of seek mentors,

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.200
do you just kind of learn
through trial and error?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.900
- A lot of trial and error,

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.770
a lot of epic mistakes.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.633
- What were some epic mistakes you made?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:16.823
- You know, just...

00:08:16.823 --> 00:08:18.650
There's 1,000.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:19.650
I mean like for example,

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.350
not understanding...

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:24.920
Not understanding the importance

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.470
of doing your own due diligence.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.260
Whether it's on hiring someone,

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:29.714
I'd be like,

00:08:29.714 --> 00:08:31.740
"Oh, they seem great, fine."

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.160
You know, you might want to check,

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:39.160
or switching email service providers.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.410
What might this entail?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.073
I had a huge problem
recently when I did that,

00:08:43.073 --> 00:08:45.160
because I just didn't do the research

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:45.993
and I didn't know.

00:08:45.993 --> 00:08:46.826
Now I know.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:49.650
- Rule number eight,
do one thing at a time.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.320
- The thing that I've learned
that's helped me the most,

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:55.700
is that I only try to
do one thing at a time.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.930
So, if I'm picking up my kids from school,

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:03.530
I'm not trying to also
make decisions about work.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.410
Because, I find that I do both badly,

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.710
so I really try to carve out my time well.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:12.040
- Rule number nine,
listen kingly and openly.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.250
- [Woman] So, you talked about the fact

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:14.930
that you've had some separation

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:15.870
between being an actress,

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.703
and being an entrepreneur.

00:09:16.703 --> 00:09:17.870
But, there must be some skills

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.490
that you're able to take
from being an actress,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.620
to becoming an entrepreneur.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.470
And I was wondering what those were?

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:23.840
- Oh, that's a really good question,

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.613
nobody's ever asked me that before.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:31.850
I think they're more interpersonal skills.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.310
Like when you're acting with somebody,

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.470
like listening, respect,

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.260
kind of being a container.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.030
I think establishing that kind of rapport,

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:45.390
and respect for people,

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.530
and listening kindly and openly.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:51.020
Those sort of skills that
help you be a good actress,

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.380
I think help you in business.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:57.398
Because, in my experience

00:09:57.398 --> 00:09:59.830
they create more points of connection,

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.260
and when you work with people,

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.990
and you have the capacity to listen,

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.105
and you have the respect back and forth,

00:10:07.105 --> 00:10:10.090
the best of that person starts to emerge.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:11.270
It's been amazing.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.710
You know, I have my girls
that I love so much.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:18.710
And to see them grow and
create roles for themselves,

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:22.150
and then fill the roles in the business,

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.380
it's amazing.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:28.380
And I do think that comes
from a very specific type

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:32.840
of listening that you learn from acting.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.260
- And rule number 10, the last one

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.062
before a very special bonus clip,

00:10:36.062 --> 00:10:37.920
is have fun.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.483
- Never ever have I lied to get a job.

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.721
- Oh, come on.

00:10:43.721 --> 00:10:45.140
- How would you lie?

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:47.390
(laughing)

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.180
- Never ever have I gotten
out of a speeding ticket

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:52.563
by being a celebrity.

00:10:53.772 --> 00:10:56.772
(audience laughing)

00:11:00.363 --> 00:11:04.523
Never ever have I forgotten
the name of a date.

00:11:05.622 --> 00:11:07.770
Like while you're with them?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.680
I don't understand that.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.360
While you're with them?

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:12.370
- While you're with them?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.554
- That would be really horrific.

00:11:14.554 --> 00:11:15.387
- Yeah.

00:11:16.287 --> 00:11:18.646
(audience laughing)

00:11:18.646 --> 00:11:20.063
- No, I've never.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.582
- Never ever have I seen
one of my Mortdecai's

00:11:26.582 --> 00:11:28.787
co-stars naked?

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:31.787
(audience cheering)

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:42.496
Never ever have I lied on a talk show.

00:11:42.496 --> 00:11:45.496
(audience laughing)

00:11:46.333 --> 00:11:47.860
- I don't believe you.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.867
It's just unbelievable.

00:11:49.867 --> 00:11:52.033
- Never ever have I sexted.

00:11:53.235 --> 00:11:54.760
(audience cheering)

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.624
- Yeah no, I haven't done that.

00:11:57.624 --> 00:12:00.624
(audience cheering)

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:03.200
- Wow.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.610
- Never ever have I said a baby was cute

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.345
when it was obviously ugly.

00:12:07.345 --> 00:12:11.070
(audience laughing)

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.300
- All right, I've got a very special

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.350
bonus clip from Gwyneth,

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.120
on how to try things,

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.530
and the importance of it that I think

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.950
you're going to really enjoy.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:18.783
But before that,

00:12:18.783 --> 00:12:20.910
it's time for the three
point landing questions.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.730
Time to move from just
watching under the video,

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:25.810
to actually taking action
in your life and business.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.710
So, here we go.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:29.090
Question number one,

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.370
how can you just start small today

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:32.870
on your big dreams?

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:36.500
Number two, what is a risk you
are going to take this week?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.246
And number three,

00:12:38.246 --> 00:12:41.733
what habits will you build in
to like yourself regularly?

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:46.610
- And I think, you know my whole

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:48.670
sort of road towards wellness,

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:50.470
started my father was
diagnosed with cancer

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.410
when I was about 26.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.090
And that's when I started reading

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.090
about environmental toxins,

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.330
and the connection
between food and cancer,

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.162
and stress and cancer.

00:13:00.162 --> 00:13:04.160
And so, I really started
to become obsessive

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.680
about in a vain effort to heal him,

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.683
kind of by proxy because he
really wasn't that interested.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.450
Health food.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:15.800
I remember I was trying to
make him go gluten free,

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:16.633
and dairy free,

00:13:16.633 --> 00:13:18.015
and sugar free,

00:13:18.015 --> 00:13:19.970
and I spent all day making these muffins,

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.040
because you know all he
wanted was to feel normal

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.680
after his cancer.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.710
I made these muffins with
I don't know coconut sugar,

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.710
and whatever kind of flour.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:31.180
And he bit into one,

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:33.380
and I was like, "What do you think?"

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.101
And he said, "It's like biting
into the New York Times."

00:13:37.101 --> 00:13:39.102
(laughing)

00:13:39.102 --> 00:13:41.350
So, he was among the first

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:46.350
who was sort of critical
of my furies into wellness.

00:13:46.637 --> 00:13:49.640
You know, I think that I remember

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.000
once I had acupuncture and cupping,

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.910
which is an ancient Chinese technique,

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.320
and there was this big
uproar in the press,

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:58.360
and I was a witch,

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.277
and what was I doing.

00:14:00.277 --> 00:14:02.964
When I starting doing yoga 20 years ago,

00:14:02.964 --> 00:14:05.278
the press had a field day with that.

00:14:05.278 --> 00:14:09.608
And I've just sort of
by pattern recognition

00:14:09.608 --> 00:14:13.530
realized that I'm somebody
who likes to try things,

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.830
and then people think I'm insane.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.200
Now there's a yoga place on every corner,

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.550
no one eats gluten anymore.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:24.200
- If I've talked to one
person who's been successful,

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:28.760
they all say at some point
people ridiculed them,

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.870
criticized them,

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:30.930
thought they were nuts,

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.270
and I think that it's really important

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.550
that if you believe in your idea,

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:38.840
if you have an ability to shut that out,

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.580
you can persevere .

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.620
- Raise your standard.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.430
- Apple at the core,

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:49.430
its core value is that we
believe that people with passion

00:14:51.852 --> 00:14:54.007
can change the world for the better.

00:14:54.007 --> 00:14:55.930
- Not one drop of my self worth

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:58.203
depends on your acceptance of me.

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:02.024
(dramatic music)

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:04.650
- If you guys liked this video,

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.170
check out the top 10
we did on Jessica Alba.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.170
It's right next to me,

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.500
I think you're going to enjoy it.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.000
Continue to believe,

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.160
and I'll see you there.

